@startuml
!include style.puml
skinparam ParticipantFontColor black
skinparam ArrowFontStyle plain

participant ":EditRoleCommand" as Command
participant ":ModelManager" as Model
participant ":AddressBook" as AddressBook
participant "roles:UniqueRoleList" as Roles
participant "persons:UniquePersonList" as Persons

note over Command
After parsing: valid positive index,
no repeated prefixes, at least one field,
valid supplied title / experience.
Parse failure never executes this sequence.
end note

[-> Command : execute(model)
Command -> Model : getFilteredRoleList()
Model --> Command : displayedRoles
alt index is outside displayedRoles
    [<-- Command : reject: invalid displayed index
else index selects a displayed role
    Command -> Command : build editedRole from selected target
    note right of Command
    Retain omitted fields and role status.
    end note

    opt !target.isSameRole(editedRole)
        Command -> Model : hasRole(editedRole)
        Model --> Command : duplicate title?
    end
    note over Command, Model
    Title identity ignores case.
    Check all roles, including closed roles.
    Case-only corrections keep the same identity.
    end note

    alt another role has the requested title
        [<-- Command : reject: duplicate role title
    else title is available or belongs to the selected role
        Command -> Model : setRole(target, editedRole)
        Model -> AddressBook : setRole(target, editedRole)
        AddressBook -> Roles : setRole(target, editedRole)
        Roles -> Roles : validate target and title uniqueness
        Roles -> Roles : replace target at its existing index
        Roles --> AddressBook

        opt title spelling changed (case-sensitive comparison)
            AddressBook -> Persons : asUnmodifiableObservableList()
            Persons --> AddressBook : all stored candidates
            loop each stored candidate (including hidden candidates)
                opt candidate's role matches old title, ignoring case
                    AddressBook -> AddressBook : copy candidate with new title\nusing candidate.withRole(newTitle)
                end
            end
            AddressBook -> Persons : setPersons(updatedPersons)
            Persons --> AddressBook
        end
        note over AddressBook, Persons
    Case-only renames also propagate. Experience-only edits skip this step.
    Preserve candidate details and order; retain unrelated instances.
        end note

        AddressBook --> Model
        Model --> Command
        [<-- Command : CommandResult
    end
end

note over Command
Rejection leaves records, filters and file unchanged.
After success, LogicManager saves both collections.
Save failures do not roll back in-memory changes.
end note
@enduml
